# Example ~/.ssh/config blocks for the Alliance clusters (copy into ~/.ssh/config on YOUR laptop;
# replace USERNAME with your Alliance username and ~/.ssh/YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY with your key).
#
# Sources (Alliance wiki, retrieved 2026-09-23, docs/agent_reports/H1_alliance_wiki.md §4):
# * Host/User/HostName/IdentityFile layout: SSH_configuration_file (example "Host narval / User
#   username / HostName narval.alliancecan.ca / IdentityFile ~/.ssh/your_private_key").
# * The three ControlPath/ControlMaster/ControlPersist lines are verbatim from
#   Multifactor_authentication § Configuring your SSH client with ControlMaster > Linux and MacOS:
#   "a first SSH session [asks] for the first and second factors, but subsequent SSH connections
#   on the same device will reuse the connection of the first session (without asking for
#   authentication), even up to 10 minutes after that first session was disconnected."
#   It does not work with native Windows (use WSL; same section).
# * Login host names: Fir § (header table); Nibi § (header table); Rorqual/en § (header table);
#   Narval/en § (header table); Trillium § (header table). Trillium_Quickstart § Logging in gives
#   trillium.scinet.utoronto.ca and trillium-gpu.scinet.utoronto.ca instead (both on the wiki;
#   H1 §8 inconsistency 4): if the alliancecan.ca names fail, use the scinet ones.
# * Trillium: "Password access to the login nodes is disabled. You must use SSH Keys and MFA."
#   (Trillium § Logging in); check the login node's host key fingerprint on first login
#   (Trillium_Quickstart § Logging in, which links SSH_security_improvements). GPU jobs must
#   be submitted from the GPU login node, so the kit's jobs on Trillium use the trillium-gpu block.
# * The wiki advises against ForwardAgent / ForwardX11 by default (SSH_configuration_file).
# * Automation (robot) nodes are NOT listed on purpose: "They are not suitable for usage of AI
#   agents" (Automation_in_the_context_of_multifactor_authentication); you run the jobs yourself.
# Register your public key in CCDB first (SSH_Keys § Using CCDB:
# https://ccdb.alliancecan.ca/ssh_authorized_keys) and your MFA device (Multifactor_authentication).

Host fir
    User USERNAME
    HostName fir.alliancecan.ca
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY
    ControlPath ~/.ssh/cm-%r@%h:%p
    ControlMaster auto
    ControlPersist 10m

Host nibi
    User USERNAME
    HostName nibi.alliancecan.ca
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY
    ControlPath ~/.ssh/cm-%r@%h:%p
    ControlMaster auto
    ControlPersist 10m

Host rorqual
    User USERNAME
    HostName rorqual.alliancecan.ca
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY
    ControlPath ~/.ssh/cm-%r@%h:%p
    ControlMaster auto
    ControlPersist 10m

Host narval
    User USERNAME
    HostName narval.alliancecan.ca
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY
    ControlPath ~/.ssh/cm-%r@%h:%p
    ControlMaster auto
    ControlPersist 10m

# Trillium CPU login nodes (setup, git, file transfers)
Host trillium
    User USERNAME
    HostName trillium.alliancecan.ca
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY
    ControlPath ~/.ssh/cm-%r@%h:%p
    ControlMaster auto
    ControlPersist 10m

# Trillium GPU login node: submit the kit's (GPU) jobs from here
Host trillium-gpu
    User USERNAME
    HostName trillium-gpu.alliancecan.ca
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY
    ControlPath ~/.ssh/cm-%r@%h:%p
    ControlMaster auto
    ControlPersist 10m
